  "rule_for_models": "Suspect a finding when the record shows a supply of Group A (an SSRI), Group B (an SNRI) or Group C (a tricyclic antidepressant at a daily dose of 50 mg or more), and supplies of at least two additional, distinct serotonergic ingredients, including the examples in Group D. Exclude tranylcypromine and the antidepressant being assessed from the partner count. All three courses must overlap at the same time, or the earliest and latest of the three supply dates must be no more than 60 days apart. Work out a tricyclic daily dose as the strength times the tablets or capsules taken each day. SSRIs and SNRIs count at any dose. If the directions leave it unclear whether the Group C dose reaches 50 mg a day and both partners qualify, cite all three supplies and report only a possible finding on that trio. Ask the patient what daily dose they take.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Whether the person really takes the medicines together, medicines bought over the counter, and doses changed outside the pharmacy. Group D is only a list of examples.",
  "ask_the_gp": "A review of whether the combination of serotonergic medicines is needed and safe, and whether any can be stopped or changed.",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": true,
  "signed_by_clinical_reviewer": null
